{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\noutput_path = Path('/Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/spaces/mind/runs/run-20260426T183154Z--3o1lqw0846/semantic/comment_section_generation/source--source-03-the-role-of-alpha-band-brain-oscillations-as-a-sensory-suppression-mechanism-dur-w2005105933--7b6b7d5bc8b9.json')\noutput_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\ndata = {\n    \\\"page_ref\\\": \\\"source:source-03-the-role-of-alpha-band-brain-oscillations-as-a-sensory-suppression-mechanism-dur-w2005105933--7b6b7d5bc8b9\\\",\n    \\\"requested_count\\\": 5,\n    \\\"comments\\\": [\n        {\n            \\\"comment_ref\\\": \\\"draft-1\\\",\n            \\\"persona_id\\\": \\\"persona-maya-santoro\\\",\n            \\\"body\\\": \\\"I like how this review turns the usual attention story around. Instead of asking only which representation gets boosted, Foxe and Snyder make a strong case that the ignored channel may need its own active control signal, with alpha rising where distracting input would otherwise compete.\\\",\n            \\\"parent_ref\\\": None,\n            \\\"score_assessment\\\": {\n                \\\"score\\\": 24,\n                \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Accurately captures the review's central suppression argument and frames it clearly without overclaiming.\\\"\n            }\n        },\n        {\n            \\\"comment_ref\\\": \\\"draft-2\\\",\n            \\\"persona_id\\\": \\\"persona-eli-okafor\\\",\n            \\\"body\\\": \\\"The bilateral rapid-stream example seems especially important because it pushes against the old cortical-idling explanation. If both visual streams are still being stimulated and alpha climbs above the pre-cue baseline for the ignored side, that looks much more like active filtering than simple recovery after stimulation.\\\",\n            \\\"parent_ref\\\": \\\"draft-1\\\",\n            \\\"score_assessment\\\": {\n                \\\"score\\\": 27,\n                \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Uses a specific evidential test from the source and explains its relevance to the active-suppression claim.\\\"\n            }\n        },\n        {\n            \\\"comment_ref\\\": \\\"draft-3\\\",\n            \\\"persona_id\\\": \\\"persona-lina-kovac\\\",\n            \\\"body\\\": \\\"One thing I would keep in view is that this is a review article, so the force of the argument depends on how consistently the cited paradigms line up. The cross-modal pattern is compelling, but it is still a synthesis rather than one unified experiment testing the whole mechanism at once.\\\",\n            \\\"parent_ref\\\": None,\n            \\\"score_assessment\\\": {\n                \\\"score\\\": 22,\n                \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Adds a useful scope caveat grounded in the source's review status while acknowledging the convergent evidence.\\\"\n            }\n        },\n        {\n            \\\"comment_ref\\\": \\\"draft-4\\\",\n            \\\"persona_id\\\": \\\"persona-rory-chen\\\",\n            \\\"body\\\": \\\"The retinotopic angle makes the claim feel more concrete to me. Alpha increasing over cortex that corresponds to the ignored hemifield is a cleaner prediction than a vague statement that attention changes oscillations somewhere in the back of the head.\\\",\n            \\\"parent_ref\\\": None,\n            \\\"score_assessment\\\": {\n                \\\"score\\\": 23,\n                \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Highlights anatomical specificity in the spatial attention evidence with a clear, source-consistent interpretation.\\\"\n            }\n        },\n        {\n            \\\"comment_ref\\\": \\\"draft-5\\\",\n            \\\"persona_id\\\": \\\"persona-samira-haddad\\\",\n            \\\"body\\\": \\\"I also appreciated that the authors do not treat all alpha as one thing. Separating attention-related alpha from arousal-related alpha makes the model less tidy, but it is probably necessary if frontal-parietal control and thalamic contributions are doing different jobs.\\\",\n            \\\"parent_ref\\\": None,\n            \\\"score_assessment\\\": {\n                \\\"score\\\": 21,\n                \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Engages the mechanism limits section thoughtfully and avoids overstating unresolved circuitry.\\\"\n            }\n        }\n    ]\n}\n\nwith output_path.open('w', encoding='utf-8') as handle:\n    json.dump(data, handle, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n    handle.write('\\\\n')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
